---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import publication from '../data/publication.json';
---

<Layout
  title="Support — Peak"
  description="Peak installation help, bug reports, privacy requests, security reports, and a guide to sharing sanitized diagnostic information."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">
        <span class="tiny-cross">+</span> A LITTLE HELP, WHEN YOU NEED IT
      </span>
      <h1>
        Let’s get you
        <br />
        back in <span class="heading-emphasis">flow.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Installation help, bug reports, privacy requests, and security concerns.
        Ordinary support is best effort.
      </p>
    </header>
    {!publication.supportEmail && (
      <div class="notice-banner">
        <Icon name="mail" />
        <div>
          <strong>Support contact is being prepared.</strong> A dedicated Gmail
          mailbox will be verified and published before the public release. No
          address has been supplied yet.
        </div>
      </div>
    )}
    <div class="page-grid">
      <div>
        <section class="content-block">
          <h2>Share a useful, sanitized report</h2>
          <p>
            Start with a short description of what you expected, what happened,
            and the steps that reproduce it. Send only the information needed to
            understand the problem.
          </p>
          <div class="report-checklist">
            <div>
              <h3>Include</h3>
              <p>
                Peak version, Windows version, provider CLI versions, Microsoft
                Store installation, the feature involved, and a minimal
                reproduction. Note whether the issue happens in demo mode.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Remove</h3>
              <p>
                Account labels, chat titles, prompts, command arguments, private
                paths, tokens, credentials, and unrelated work. Crop screenshots
                to the relevant interface.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            Do not send complete provider transcripts, raw session logs,
            credential stores, <code>auth.json</code>, or restoration backups.
            Peak never automatically uploads diagnostics. If additional
            information is needed, support can explain how to share a smaller
            sanitized example.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="content-block">
          <h2>A few checks before you write</h2>
          <h3>The island is hidden</h3>
          <p>
            Try the default reveal shortcut, <code>Ctrl+Alt+U</code>, or choose{' '}
            <strong>Show details</strong> from the tray. A saved alternative
            shortcut, presence mode, pointer fading, or fullscreen setting can
            change visibility.
          </p>
          <h3>Usage is unavailable or stale</h3>
          <p>
            Check that the provider is enabled and its compatible CLI is
            installed and signed in. Codex requires a usable Windows credential
            store. Claude refreshes usage during CLI activity. A dash is unknown
            data, not zero usage.
          </p>
          <h3>Codex review requests are missing</h3>
          <p>
            Check hook support and trust in Codex, then reconnect the chat.
            Managed restrictions, remote execution, or unsupported hooks can
            prevent observations. Peak never grants hook trust or changes
            approval policies.
          </p>
          <h3>Screen sharing still captures Peak</h3>
          <p>
            Capture exclusion depends on the recording tool. Check an actual
            capture before sharing; do not rely on it as a universal guarantee.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href="/download/#setup">Full setup instructions</a>
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="content-block">
          <h2>Privacy and security reports</h2>
          <p>
            Use the same support mailbox for requests to access, correct, or
            delete publisher-held support information. Identify the
            correspondence involved without including unnecessary private data.
            Applicable privacy deadlines take precedence over ordinary support
            handling.
          </p>
          <p>
            For a security concern, use a clear subject such as “Peak security
            report,” describe the affected version and impact, and provide a
            sanitized reproduction. Avoid public disclosure of credentials or
            another person’s data.
          </p>
          <h3>Support correspondence</h3>
          <p>
            The default is to delete resolved correspondence after 90 days,
            except records required for an ongoing dispute or legal obligation.
            Unresolved issues are kept while being handled. See the privacy
            notice for hosting and mailbox processing.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
      <aside class="page-aside">
        <div class="aside-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">CONTACT</span>
          <h2>
            One mailbox.
            <br />A direct conversation.
          </h2>
          {publication.supportEmail ? (
            <>
              <p>{publication.supportEmail}</p>
              <a
                class="button button-primary"
                href={`mailto:${publication.supportEmail}`}
              >
                Email Peak support <Icon name="mail" size={16} />
              </a>
            </>
          ) : (
            <p>The verified support email will appear here before launch.</p>
          )}
          <p>No contact form, account, or automatic attachment upload.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="aside-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">HELPFUL LINKS</span>
          <div class="aside-links">
            <a href="/download/">Downloads & setup ↗</a>
            <a href="/privacy/">Privacy ↗</a>
            <a href="/terms/">Freeware terms ↗</a>
            <a href="/#playground">Try the sample playground ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
